  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1095-overtaking-orders",
      "source_numbers": ["1095"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "第一名旅行者以 $4$ 千米/小时从 $A$ 出发，$1$ 小时后第二名以 $5$ 千米/小时从 $A$ 出发；再过 $1$ 小时，骑车者从 $A$ 出发。各自速度保持不变，路线足够长使两次超车都能发生。骑车者超过其中一人后，$10$ 分钟又超过另一人，没有规定先超过哪一人。骑车速度的全部可能值是哪一组？",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "A", "text": "$\\{7,20\\}$ 千米/小时", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "B", "text": "$\\{20\\}$ 千米/小时", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "C", "text": "$\\left\\{\\dfrac{-9+\\sqrt{481}}2,7,20\\right\\}$ 千米/小时", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "D", "text": "$\\left\\{\\dfrac{-9-\\sqrt{481}}2,\\dfrac{-9+\\sqrt{481}}2,7,20\\right\\}$ 千米/小时", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Find all positive bicycle speeds consistent with both possible overtaking orders and10-minute separation.",
        "source_solution": "At bicycle start the walkers lead8 and5 km. Forv>5,catch times t4=8/(v-4),t5=5/(v-5). Witht4-t5=1/6, v^2-27v+140=0 gives7,20, both>20/3. Witht5-t4=1/6,v^2+9v-100=0 gives(-9+sqrt481)/2 in(5,20/3); the negative root is discarded. Thus three possible speeds remain.",
        "unit_reason": "One complete speed set preserves the unspecified overtaking order and both branches, rather than silently choosing the5 km/h walker as the first caught.",
        "concept_blocks": [],
        "limitations": ["Selecting the complete set does not demonstrate producing both signed catch-time equations.", "Uniform speeds and a route long enough for the actual catches are explicit model qualifications. No original numerical AB length or unique overtaking order is recovered."],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["C"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "A", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "7 and20 solve the branch catching the5 km/h walker first, but the other order gives(-9+sqrt481)/2>5 and is also admissible.", "misconception": "Replace the absolute catch-time difference by t4-t5=1/6 alone and omit the opposite overtaking order."},
          {"option_id": "B", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "20 is valid, but7 has catch times5/2 and8/3 with difference1/6, and the opposite order also gives a third speed.", "misconception": "Choose the plus root20 of the first-order quadratic, discarding its minus root7 and never examining reversed order."},
          {"option_id": "C", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "Both signed-order quadratics are exhausted.7,20 meetv>20/3 for t4>t5;(-9+sqrt481)/2 is between5 and20/3 for t5>t4. Each meets its order and10-minute separation.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "D", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "The extra root(-9-sqrt481)/2 is negative, cannot travel toward the walkers or overtake them, and violatesv>5.", "misconception": "Collect every algebraic root of both quadratics without enforcing positive speed and thecatch-time domains."}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q1096-skating-all-results",
      "source_numbers": ["1096"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "两名运动员同时开始 $10000$ 米滑冰训练，第一人比第二人快 $\\frac13$ 米/秒，每圈用时少 $2$ 秒。$10$ 分钟后，第一人实际领先第二人半圈。两人各保持自己的速度不变。哪一项同时给出两人的正确速度和滑完整程的时间？各项时间都用秒表示。",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "A", "text": "第一人 $75$ 米/秒、$\\frac{400}{3}$ 秒；第二人 $72$ 米/秒、$\\frac{1250}{9}$ 秒。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "B", "text": "第一人 $\\frac{25}{3}$ 米/秒、$1200$ 秒；第二人 $8$ 米/秒、$1250$ 秒。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "C", "text": "第一人 $\\frac{\\sqrt{1201}+1}{6}$ 米/秒、$50(\\sqrt{1201}-1)$ 秒；第二人 $\\frac{\\sqrt{1201}-1}{6}$ 米/秒、$50(\\sqrt{1201}+1)$ 秒。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "D", "text": "第一人 $-8$ 米/秒、$-1250$ 秒；第二人 $-\\frac{25}{3}$ 米/秒、$-1200$ 秒。", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Determine both speeds and both full-distance times consistently with half-lap gain and per-lap difference.",
        "source_solution": "In600s thegain is200m,so laplength400m. With slowerv,400/v-400/(v+1/3)=2 gives3v^2+v-200=0 andv=8 after rejecting-25/3. Faster25/3. Fulltimes10000/(25/3)=1200s=20min and10000/8=1250s=20min50s.",
        "unit_reason": "One complete ordered result combines speed inference, lap geometry, role identity and both requested full-route times. Different candidate speed pairs prevent inheriting the correct speeds from every option; both positive gap-correct candidates have internally consistent times, so their distinction still requires the lap data.",
        "concept_blocks": [],
        "limitations": ["Complete-result recognition does not demonstrate independently deriving the lap length and quadratic.", "Unchanged speeds and actual accumulated half-lap gain are explicit model qualifications, not a recovered modulo-lap ambiguity."],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["B"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "A", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Misread the gap as3:600*3=1800m half-lap gain gives lap3600; uv=3600*3/2=5400,u-v=3 yields u75,v72. Their full times400/3s and1250/9s match those mistaken speeds, but75-72=3 differs from the given1/3.", "misconception": "Invert the fractional speed gap1/3 to3 before using the remaining lap relationships."},
          {"option_id": "B", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "Speeds differ by1/3,lap times48s and50s differ by2,and600s gain is200m.10000m times are1200s and1250s in the stated order.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "C", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Treat the200m gain as a full lap: uv=200*(1/3)/2=100/3 andu-v=1/3 give3v^2+v-100=0, hence the displayed positive radical pair. Rationalizing10000/u and10000/v gives50*(sqrt1201-1) and50*(sqrt1201+1). Actual half-lap gain requires lap400, where these speeds give400*(1/3)/(100/3)=4s lap-time difference, not2s.", "misconception": "Use the accumulated half-lap lead as one complete lap length, omitting the factor2."},
          {"option_id": "D", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Keeping the actual quadratic's rootv=-25/3 givesu=-8 and times10000/(-8)=-1250s,10000/(-25/3)=-1200s. Algebraic difference1/3 remains, but negative speed/time violates the physical domain.", "misconception": "Keep the negative quadratic root instead of requiring positive skating speeds and elapsed times."}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q1097-perpendicular-travel-times",
      "source_numbers": ["1097"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "骑车者和摩托车手沿相互垂直的直路行驶，开始时分别在交叉路口前方 $8$ 千米、$15$ 千米处，速度分别为 $\\frac13$ 千米/分、$1$ 千米/分。两人均保持速度沿原直路穿过路口继续前行。经过多少分钟，两人间的距离等于 $5$ 千米？选择全部时刻组成的集合。",
