          {"option_id": "B", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "1/5+1/(10/3)=1/2,so meeting occurs2h after simultaneous start;5-10/3=5/3 hours with the first later.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "C", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "The difference4-7/3=5/3 is correct,but1/4+3/7=19/28,not1/2,so the2h meeting fails.", "misconception": "Assume meeting occurs at each traveler's halfway point,set first full time2*2=4,and subtract the arrival delay for the second."},
          {"option_id": "D", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "11/3-2=5/3,but3/11+1/2=17/22,not1/2. Treating2h as the second's complete journey contradicts the meeting-rate data.", "misconception": "Set the earlier traveler's full-route time equal to the meeting time2h,then add1h40min for the first."}
